# vergeio_tenant_copy (Resource)

Copies a tenant and keeps the copy in state. Destroy deletes the copy. The source tenant and `snapshot_id` are only read.

The pinned govergeos client clones a tenant with `Tenants.Clone`. That call takes `name`, `no_vnet`, `no_storage`, and `no_nodes`. It has no snapshot argument, so the copy is the current tenant. `snapshot_id` must be a `tenant_snapshots` row of `tenant_id`. The `tenant_actions` `restore` action sends `params.snapshot` and overwrites that tenant. This resource does not call it. A system snapshot can create a new tenant through `cloud_snapshot_tenant_actions` action `recover`. The pinned client does not expose that call.

`isolate` defaults to true and posts `isolateon` on the copy when it is not already isolated. This resource does not post `isolateoff`. Set `isolate` to false to keep the connectivity the clone copied.

This is not the [`vergeio_tenant_clone` action](../actions/tenant_clone.html). That action copies a tenant and does not keep the copy in state.

